WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.000
All praise is due to Allah, we praise Him, we worship Him, we ask His forgiveness.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
And we seek refuge with Allah from the evil of our souls and from the evil of our deeds.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Whoever guides him, Allah will not harm him, and whoever guides him, Allah will not harm him.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.000
And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone.

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
And I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.000
O you who believe, fear Allah and do not die except when you are Muslim.

8
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.636
O you people, fear your Lord who created you from one soul and

9
00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:39.000
created your wife from it.

10
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:46.000
And only from them are there many men and women. And fear Allah who ask for him and the mercy.

11
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Indeed, Allah is kind to you. O you who believe, fear Allah and say a wise saying

12
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.000
that will help you do good deeds and forgive you your sins.

13
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.000
And whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has a great success.

14
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.000
As for the next one, the book of Allah is the best.

15
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.000
And the best gift is the gift of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him.

16
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.000
And the evil is for its events. And every event is a sacrifice. And every sacrifice is a injustice.

17
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.000
And every injustice is in the fire.

18
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Brothers and sisters, I would like to welcome you to the first of our classes

19
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.000
of the explanation of the Kitab al-Tawheed by Sheikh Muhammad Ibn Abdul Wahhab

20
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:33.200
on this seventh day of June in the year 1999, corresponding to

21
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.000
the 22nd of Safar, 1420 of the Hijrah.

22
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:44.000
And I would like to first and foremost congratulate you for choosing this type of experience

23
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.000
for opting to undergo an intensive series of Islamic lectures and courses, insha'Allah,

24
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:56.000
for the next two or three weeks. And I say that, insha'Allah, may Allah SWT reward you with sincerity

25
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.000
and reward you with good in this life and the hereafter.

26
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:05.000
And may He make this series of lectures a means of baraka, a means of good for us in this life

27
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:10.000
so that we can worship Allah upon a balsira, upon a clear light, upon a clear vision

28
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:16.000
and so that we may then attain the fruits of this worship in the hereafter by obtaining jannah, insha'Allah.

29
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.000
And I would like to point out that this book, Kitab al-Tawheed in my opinion

30
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
is one of the most practical and beneficial books to study in our time.

31
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.000
And that the author, Muhammad Ibn Abdul Wahhab, he compiled in this book a series

32
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
or a group of Qur'anic ayat and a hadith that are related to each other

33
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.000
all concerning the topic of Tawheed which we will talk about in a short while.

34
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Now the author, his full name is Muhammad Ibn Abdul Wahhab Ibn Sulaiman from the tribe of Wahhabi.

35
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.000
And he was born in the year 1115 of the Hijrah.

36
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:59.000
Right now in the year 1420 he was born 1115 of the Hijrah which is around 300 or so years ago.

37
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:03.000
And he was born in the city of Dar'iyya in Saudi Arabia.

38
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.000
Well at that time it was called Arabia, it wasn't called Saudi Arabia.

39
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.000
And he lived a life of knowledge in the sense that his father and his grandfather

40
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.000
and his tribe was well known for knowledge. So he memorized the Qur'an when he was young

41
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.000
and he studied under many of the famous Shuyukh or the scholars of his time.

42
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.000
However he noticed that in his country, in Arabia of his time,

43
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.000
there was a lot of shirk, there was a lot of grave worship,

44
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.000
there was a lot of acts that were prohibited by the Sharia and by Islam.

45
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:35.000
So he started calling the people away from these types of acts

46
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:42.000
and calling him to the pure worship of Allah SWT. Allah SWT blessed a certain person, a certain leader,

47
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.000
a certain ruler of that time to accept his da'wah, to accept his call

48
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.000
so that this ruler then joined ranks with Muhammed Ibn Al-Wahab

49
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.000
and together they managed to unify the Arabia of their time

50
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.000
and also to prevent and prohibit these people from the types of shirk

51
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:04.000
and the types of inhibitions that they were doing. Now Muhammed Ibn Al-Wahab, the person himself,

52
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:10.000
almost everyone has heard of him. He is either loved or hated by almost everyone today.

53
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.000
He is either loved or hated. His enemies hate him and the people that know the Sunnah, they love him.

54
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.000
And I'd like to point out to you that this book of his,

55
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.000
Kitabat al-Hait, is considered to be one of the spearhead books

56
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.000
that he used in his quote-unquote revolution or his quote-unquote

57
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.000
renovation, not innovation but renovation of the religion of Islam.

58
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.000
He renovated the religion of Islam, in other words, Tajdeed.

59
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.000
He brought it back to the original roots that it was.

60
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.000
Now the reason we're going to study this book in particular,

61
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:43.000
while we study this book, I want you to have a very open mind, a very clear mind and see for yourselves

62
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:47.000
how much did the author himself speak and how much he let Allah and His messengers speak.

63
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:52.000
And see for yourselves, is Muhammed Ibn Al-Wahab calling to something which is new

64
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.000
or calling to something which has existed for thousands and thousands of years.

65
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:02.000
And you will see, inshallah, that the author in this book, he rarely says anything.

66
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:08.000
All he says is Allah says this and His messenger says that and Allah says this and His messenger says that.

67
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.000
So how can it be then that a person opposes these types of teachings?

68
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:17.000
Muhammed Ibn Al-Wahab, the person, we don't exalt or glorify him or put him above his status.

69
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.000
No, he was a human being, he lived and he died.

70
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.000
So we don't worship him, we don't exalt him, nothing of this nature.

71
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.000
However, we say to those that oppose his message, not in defense of the personality of this person,

72
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:34.000
but in defense of his teachings, we say to them, what you are opposing is the truth.

73
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.000
And like we pointed out, like we say over and over again,

74
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:43.000
a person only has to study the teachings of this person and the teachings of the people before him

75
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.000
and the ones after him to realize that he did not come forth with something new.

76
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:52.000
He was not the leader of a group. He was not the one who founded this group or founded this movement.

77
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.000
Unlike many of the movements that exist today that have specific founders, no.

78
00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:59.000
And this book that we are going to study today, inshallah, will clearly prove that.

79
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.000
And I want you, like I said, if anyone has any doubts in his mind,

80
00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.000
fine, attend these classes and see for yourselves

81
00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:09.000
how much did Muhammad Ibn Aghwahab himself add or subtract from this religion?

82
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.000
Or did he just present the religion again?

83
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.000
Did he just present the Quranic Ayat and the hadith pertaining to Tawheed

84
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.000
and pertaining to the true worship of Allah SWT?

85
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.000
And the da'wah that Allah SWT did through his hand was a blessed da'wah.

86
00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.000
And because of this, the whole continent or the whole peninsula of Arabia

87
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:30.000
returned back to Tawheed after it was immersed in the concept of shirk,

88
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.000
of grave worship, of worshiping, of dead saints, of blindly following people.

89
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.000
When Muhammad Ibn Aghwahab came, he renovated the whole region of Islam again

90
00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:44.000
in this peninsula, in this continent. And because of that, he was opposed by many of the people of his time.

91
00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.000
He was opposed specifically by the people who were in power

92
00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:51.000
because they felt that his da'wah would be a threat to their power.

93
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.000
His da'wah would be a threat to their stability.

94
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.000
So they opposed him and they got the help of the British against him.

95
00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:04.000
And this is a long historical, you know, the history of it. We don't want to get involved in it.

96
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.000
But insha'Allah, the gist of it was by the time that he passed away,

97
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:12.000
Alhamdulillah, Allah SWT caused his da'wah to be accepted by the people. And how could it not be accepted?

98
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.000
Because there was only a call to the return of the Quran and Sunnah.

99
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:21.000
It was only, if you like, a rejuvenation, if you like, of the real religion of Islam.

100
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:27.000
And after it had been for a long time, covered up by a lot of lies and deceits by the scholars of his time.

101
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:34.000
Muhammad bin Abdul Wahab passed away in the year 1207, I believe.

102
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:40.000
In the year 1207 and 1206, excuse me, at the age of 91,

103
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.000
a very ripe, Alhamdulillah, very full life he lived,

104
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:48.000
he passed away in the year 1206 Hijriya in the city of Riyadh.

105
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:54.000
His, like we said, is one of his most important works. And insha'Allah, we will study it chapter by chapter,

106
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.000
sentence by sentence, word by word,

107
00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.000
so that insha'Allah, when you finish from these three and a half or four weeks,

108
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.000
you will have a pure, total understanding of this work,

109
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:07.000
which, like we said, is composed of only Quranic Ayat and Ahadith. It doesn't say anything of his.

110
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.000
All it is is Quranic Ayat and Ahadith. All he did was compile it into this specific book

111
00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:17.000
and put chapters on top of it. Now, the system we're going to use in explaining the book

112
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.000
is that I'm going to ask Brother Hood to read every section of the book,

113
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:23.000
every verse or every hadith, one by one, when we get to that section.

114
00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.000
And this is a system which is well-known amongst the scholars,

115
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.000
is that this is the way that they explain the book,

116
00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:33.000
is that one of the persons, he reads the book to the person that is going to explain it, point by point,

117
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:38.000
and then the person, he gives an explanation of what was read to him. Now, this has a number of benefits.

118
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:43.000
Firstly and foremost, it makes it clear in the minds of the audience what is the text of the book

119
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.000
and what is the explanation by the person who is giving the explanation.

120
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.000
And the problem that I noticed is that I've explained this book a number of times before in English

121
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:55.000
is that people would get confused between what the author himself said and what the explanation was,

122
00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:59.000
because the explanation obviously also contains Quran and Hadith. So in order to remove that problem,

123
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:03.000
is that what I've asked Brother Hood to do is that he's going to read to me the book,

124
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.000
point by point, Hadith by Hadith, Aya by Aya.

125
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.000
And then whatever he reads, you know that that is part of the book.

126
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:12.000
And inshallah, you'll have a copy of the book in front of you so that you can also go back to that.

127
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.000
And whatever I say is the explanation of the book.

128
00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:20.000
So you can make a clear differentiation between the actual book and then the actual explanation of the book.

129
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:25.000
With that, we say, Bismillah ar-Rahman ar-Rahim. Qitaab al-Tawheed.

130
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:31.000
Okay, the author entitled his book, Qitaab al-Tawheed, or the book of Tawheed.

131
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.000
Now what is the meaning of the word Tawheed?

132
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:39.000
Tawheed is based from the root word Wahada.

133
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.000
Tawheed is based from the root word Wahada.

134
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:51.000
Wahada means to ascribe unity to something.

135
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:57.000
To ascribe unity to an object. Wahada means to ascribe unity to something.

136
00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:00.000
So he made something or some concept or some person, one.

137
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.000
So Tawheed then is the act of ascribing unity to something.

138
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:12.000
And when it comes to Islamic sciences, this was the linguistic definition, when it comes to Islamic sciences,

139
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:19.000
Tawheed refers to the unification of Allah SWT. If you like the uniqueness of Allah SWT,

140
00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:26.000
when it comes to his lordship, his right to be worshipped, and his names and attributes.

141
00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:32.000
So Tawheed then is that we single out Allah. We make Allah SWT unique.

142
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:37.000
We make Allah SWT one in three concepts, in three aspects.

143
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:41.000
The first one was Tawheed of lordship. And in Arabic this is called,

144
00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:45.000
and I want you to write down these Arabic terms. Some basic Arabic terms I'm going to dictate to you.

145
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:50.000
Tawheed al-Rububiyyah. Tawheed al-Rububiyyah.

146
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:57.000
Tawheed of lordship. Tawheed al-Rububiyyah. This classification of Tawheed

147
00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:03.000
or this categorization of Tawheed is obviously based on the Qur'an and the Sunnah.

148
00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:09.000
The meaning of Tawheed al-Rububiyyah is that Allah SWT is one

149
00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:15.000
in the fact that he is the only one who created all of mankind and all of the creation.

150
00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:19.000
And he is the only one who sustains all of mankind and all of the creation.

151
00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:25.000
And he is the only one who has control of all of the creation. So in other words,

152
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:31.000
if someone were to ask you who is your creator you would respond Allah SWT and this is Tawheed al-Rububiyyah.

153
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:36.000
In other words, the fact that we only have one creator and one sustainer and one nourisher

154
00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:42.000
and one deity who is in charge of the affairs of all of the creation. Only one. This is based on the Arabic

155
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:48.000
Wulut Rabb, meaning the Lord. You say Ya Rabb, O my Lord. From the same root is Tawheed al-Rububiyyah

156
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:52.000
is that the unity of lordship. Insha'Allah we will discuss Tawheed al-Rububiyyah

157
00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:56.000
in more detail in the weekend section or in the weekend sessions that we have on the Arkham.

158
00:11:56.000 --> 00:12:02.000
The second category of Tawheed al-Rububiyyah we mentioned is Tawheed al-Rubiyyah. Tawheed al-Rubiyyah.

159
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:08.000
Tawheed al-Rububiyyah, Tawheed of worship. The second category of Tawheed is Tawheed al-Rubiyyah

160
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:14.000
or the Tawheed of worship. Brother, there is a space over there if you want.

161
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:20.000
I think there is some left too. The Tawheed of worship. What this entails

162
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:26.000
this is the natural follow up of Tawheed al-Rububiyyah. Once you have acknowledged that

163
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:32.000
Allah SWT is your creator and your only creator Allah SWT is your sustainer

164
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:38.000
and nourisher and the one that gives you your life and your food and everything the logical consequence

165
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:44.000
or the logical follow up from that is that you worship only Allah SWT You can't take another one from Tawheed.

166
00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:50.000
There is one back there. The logical consequence or the follow up of that

167
00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:54.000
is that you acknowledge that only Allah SWT has the right to be worshiped

168
00:12:54.000 --> 00:13:00.000
and this is called Tawheed al-Rububiyyah that the Tawheed means worship.

169
00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:06.000
The last category of Tawheed is the Tawheed of Names and Attributes of Allah Tawheed of Asma'i wa Srifat

170
00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:12.000
Asma' means names Srifat means attributes. The Tawheed of Names and Attributes of Allah

171
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:18.000
Tawheed of Asma'i wa Srifat Names and Attributes Now what does this mean?

172
00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:24.000
Again this is a logical follow up from Rububiyyah A logical follow up from Rububiyyah

173
00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:30.000
If you have acknowledged that Allah SWT is the only creator this automatically implies that Allah SWT

174
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:36.000
is blessed with certain attributes certain qualities that are perfect

175
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:42.000
and cannot be if you like they are perfect, they are flawless they are the ones that befit Allah SWT

176
00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:48.000
for example the attribute of creation the attribute of knowledge the attribute of power

177
00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:52.000
the attribute of every single perfect attribute it belongs to Allah SWT

178
00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:58.000
this is the Tawheed of Asma'i wa Srifat Allah SWT those perfect names and attributes

179
00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:04.000
that are found in the Quran and Sunnah and we deny from Allah SWT every negative attribute

180
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:10.000
we say Allah is free of this attribute again found in the Quran and Sunnah so for example Allah SWT

181
00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:16.000
affirms for himself that the ever merciful and the bestower of mercy

182
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:22.000
that the one who knows the unseen he calls himself Allah which is one of the names of Allah

183
00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:28.000
and we are going to discuss this name insha'Allah in a little while he calls himself

184
00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:34.000
the one who forgives the ever merciful so on and so forth

185
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:40.000
all of these names and attributes they form a part of Tawheed of Asma'i wa Srifat that we affirm for Allah SWT

186
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:46.000
everything that he affirmed for himself and we deny from him all negative attributes

187
00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:52.000
so Allah SWT has denied from himself sleep he says Allah SWT neither does slumber overtake him

188
00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:58.000
nor sleep he has also denied for himself having a son or a wife

189
00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:04.000
and he has denied this in very strong terms in the Quran which is what the Christians accuse him of

190
00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:10.000
so Allah SWT denies this because this is an imperfect attribute so this comes under Tawheed

191
00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:16.000
that Asma'i wa Srifat now realize that most of mankind

192
00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:22.000
majority of mankind they accepted Tawheed al-Rububiyyah

